# Content & Privacy

## Writing rule

Reader-facing text under `content/` is typed by the author. Agents may create empty scaffolds (frontmatter, title, `<!-- write here -->`). They must not draft, edit, polish, or translate sentences, and must not fill a scaffold because a page looks bare. A `description` longer than two sentences or twenty words stays empty. See [`human-prose.mdc`](human-prose.mdc).

## File layout

| Locale | Blog | Pages |
|--------|------|-------|
| EN | `content/blog/*.md` | `content/pages/*.md` |
| DE | `content/de/blog/*.md` | `content/de/pages/*.md` |

Schema defined in `content.config.ts`. Blog posts support `draft: true` (hidden from listing).

## Frontmatter

**Blog**: `title`, `description`, `date`, `tags`, `draft`
**Pages**: `title`, `description`, `draft`

Set `draft: true` until the author confirms publish. Blog listings hide drafts.

## Privacy — never commit

Content in git is public-facing — including `draft: true` posts. The same rules apply to every markdown file in the repo.

- Real company name, address, employees, customers, suppliers
- Private manufacturing app names, ERP/RPS data, production figures
- Anything identifying a specific business or person

See [`.cursor/public-repo-standards.md`](../public-repo-standards.md).

## When unsure

Ask the author before including a detail that could identify a person or a business. **WERKSCODE** may appear as the public name.
